> What do you mean by "possibly crashing" ?

@Gallilus I mean if the `Ref<Script> script`'s private`Script *reference` member is indeed `nullptr` then `script->is_valid()` is equivalent to `nullptr->is_valid()`. And dereferencing `nullptr` is an undefined behavior, might result in a crash.

Hence before any `script->...` calls it should be ensured (e.g. by calling `script.is_valid()`) that it can be dereferenced.

